{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_42febe8e6d99ab2464dfd452a0620b84430fa96b0e2fc0a0ebaeb7fbda9fda4e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Intel macOS wheels are no longer published because cryptography 49.0.0+ ships no Intel-macOS wheel and CAO requires cryptography>=50.0.0, so Intel Macs cannot resolve dependencies."},{"claim_ids":["clm_50bae23659e17f11e1e05ab011e1a0b3211155a5fbdb692e6399da4e3b8d6341"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Multiple agent CLI providers are supported, including MiniMax Code (mcode), Oh My Pi (omp), xAI Grok Build CLI (grok_cli), Cursor CLI, and Antigravity CLI (agy)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69523683b861008c7f526f19d0f8f59b04f5515ad335328c60394bee829316ae"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The system includes a memory layer with typed relationship storage, memory plugins for Claude Code, Kiro, and Codex, and a wiki with self-healing via 'cao memory heal'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_85accfa3635dbc0d6bb6a30a9b7610cda1d1a48bedf3564256ac339a2bf44158"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"CLI commands cao agent assign|handoff|send-message|status|result|cancel exist as a fallback when a terminal's MCP connection is unavailable, sharing an orchestration module with the MCP tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d25ac339bc8aaca4df03f77e80eff23628a1b57aec6449aeb7abf6040f94ad2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project floors at cryptography>=50.0.0 for two HIGH CVEs, pins nanoid >=3.3.17 via npm overrides for CVE-2026-67213, and bumped mcp to 1.28.1."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9661057684772b4e36c1d48a8e66bcf421f824910fc9a5314af36046298677a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions run in tmux terminals with a conductor concept: a session's first (oldest surviving) terminal is normally its conductor, and five consumers depend on that ordering."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a80ea9bd8bd3a66107d0d5094eef74417946ee52ab145020187f3007b2f6dcfa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Windows is unsupported: the backend is tmux and four modules import fcntl at module scope, so the package refuses Windows at import with an explanation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c33855e07578e7ef161b073222344ed2eec5cdecd8c3a8199c9ad05b46a0f011"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The grok_cli provider offers native hard tool restrictions, and network egress is gated behind a web_fetch tool category; per-role tool-restriction examples are provided."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c578c9d5ca7ae4a8d504951834f86b58a5d60ded544d51d10977f80b89268576"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An opt-in self-learning loop captures outcomes, performs retrospection, and promotes instructions; a skills/cao-learning skill instructs agents how to use it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d189db69298b2c94bfcfbe1dfba26deb49145a48e92291fb4ab1784a3ef105f7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project ships a cao-mcp-server that exposes orchestration tools such as assign, handoff, report_outcome, list_outcomes, and store_lesson to agents over MCP."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d2fdee6cac98916e1c7ef790ca23600d607ced0aaea22ee8c2ad45213cf20ad7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Orchestration includes supervisor/worker flows, a run engine with durable run journal and playback, frozen execution manifests with plan approval, and a cross-node fleet coordinator."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc8d937d761bfacf4e1a4e1031788b4c4ebcd22d15c68c07d742252ea8a6b4bc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Web UI provides a Profiles tab for browsing, creating, editing, cloning, and deleting agent profiles over profile management APIs, plus memory-system and fleet-panel views."}],"claim_ids":["clm_42febe8e6d99ab2464dfd452a0620b84430fa96b0e2fc0a0ebaeb7fbda9fda4e","clm_50bae23659e17f11e1e05ab011e1a0b3211155a5fbdb692e6399da4e3b8d6341","clm_69523683b861008c7f526f19d0f8f59b04f5515ad335328c60394bee829316ae","clm_85accfa3635dbc0d6bb6a30a9b7610cda1d1a48bedf3564256ac339a2bf44158","clm_8d25ac339bc8aaca4df03f77e80eff23628a1b57aec6449aeb7abf6040f94ad2","clm_9661057684772b4e36c1d48a8e66bcf421f824910fc9a5314af36046298677a4","clm_a80ea9bd8bd3a66107d0d5094eef74417946ee52ab145020187f3007b2f6dcfa","clm_c33855e07578e7ef161b073222344ed2eec5cdecd8c3a8199c9ad05b46a0f011","clm_c578c9d5ca7ae4a8d504951834f86b58a5d60ded544d51d10977f80b89268576","clm_d189db69298b2c94bfcfbe1dfba26deb49145a48e92291fb4ab1784a3ef105f7","clm_d2fdee6cac98916e1c7ef790ca23600d607ced0aaea22ee8c2ad45213cf20ad7","clm_fc8d937d761bfacf4e1a4e1031788b4c4ebcd22d15c68c07d742252ea8a6b4bc"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:40Z","created_by_operation":"op_2d92f8242c834dde82525719c0e2de71","id":"pg_e13dc9a89e065ac58f928a81cab5a12c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/awslabs-cli-agent-orchestrator-changelog-md-948c3d8004fa-8a81cab5a12c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_74f324e69b0d55e3a7d548c455f19056"],"title":"awslabs/cli-agent-orchestrator/CHANGELOG.md @ 948c3d8004fa","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:36:40Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2d92f8242c834dde82525719c0e2de71"}
